WEBVTT

00:00:57.919 --> 00:01:00.645
I like to think of the movies
and shows I create

00:01:00.669 --> 00:01:03.116
as a kind of visual medicine.

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:06.007
By that I mean I try to put
stories on the screen

00:01:06.031 --> 00:01:08.223
that address large social barriers,

00:01:08.247 --> 00:01:10.313
like racism in America,

00:01:10.337 --> 00:01:11.953
gender inequities in Ethiopia

00:01:11.977 --> 00:01:14.022
and global health disparities.

00:01:14.046 --> 00:01:18.169
And it's always my hope that audiences
leave inspired to take actions

00:01:18.193 --> 00:01:20.814
that will help people
hurdle those barriers.

00:01:21.151 --> 00:01:22.701
Visual medicine.

00:01:23.443 --> 00:01:26.099
Most of the time,
I live and work in Ethiopia,

00:01:26.123 --> 00:01:27.693
the country I was born in,

00:01:27.717 --> 00:01:30.464
and currently,
I sit on the advisory council